      "result": {
        "submission": "update-stage33.json",
        "summary": "No new work is claimed: about three minutes of the run's total budget remain, every question in the record is locally answered or explicitly bounded, there are no open necessary gaps, and I am not manufacturing a marginal item to fill the interval. The path returned is the last accepted draft, unchanged, so the controller records no_change rather than a duplicate revision.\n\nThe record stands as delivered across this run, all receipt-backed or source-cited:\n\nConfirmed defects. A leadership-transfer order is accepted with no authority binding (no term in the message, no check of sender identity, term or membership, while the order also suppresses pre-vote and the known-leader vote rejection; one order from a non-member claimed sender deposed a serving leader against an unchanged stale-term RequestVote control). `GetConfiguration().Index()` returns a constant zero, and because the `prevIndex` guard only fires for non-zero values a change guarded with the value the API returned is applied after an intervening change, while the genuine-index control is rejected. A node recovered through InstallSnapshot keeps its log store index below the snapshot index, making `shouldSnapshot`'s unsigned delta permanently true, so it rewrites an identical full-state snapshot every SnapshotInterval while idle (two executions, 15 and 13 distinct IDs at one index, versus 1 for the leader control).\n\nConditional finding. A below-protocol-2 leader writes membership changes in the deprecated voter-only peer format, and the constructor restores versioned configurations regardless of protocol version, so a rollback-style deployment can silently drop non-voting members; quorum cannot be lost and the library neither prevents nor warns about that rollback.\n\nNegative results with their boundaries: snapshot recency enforced only by term (with a control-backed run showing no applied-index regression), a stranded leader's `VerifyLeader` completing with an error in the order of the leader lease, `ReloadConfig` rejecting a constructor-invalid merge without changing anything, configuration propagation converging in 25 of 25 rounds with no node publishing stale membership while holding the entry, pipelined replication's optimistic cursor never becoming acknowledged state, the heartbeat fast path's lock-protected mutation set, and the documented contracts for log-store gaps, barriers, progress accessors, shutdown ordering, observation delivery, batching apply, RPC version admission and existing-state detection.\n\nUnresolved boundaries are recorded rather than smoothed over: the un-reproduced local failure of the captured upgrade test, and the heartbeat fast path being unexecutable in this run's isolation because no network namespace is available."
      },
